{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"ui/resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Explains what one session cost and why: token totals (uncached input, cache write, cache read, reasoning, output) and AI Credits, each with turn coverage; cache hit ratio; spend per model; the most expensive turns; cost-relevant events (compaction, cache expiry, model switch, ...); and context overhead (system-prompt parts, tools defined but never used); the session's repository and project; `subagents` (the runs and their total) when the session's totals include subagent runs: AI Credits for Copilot Chat; tokens and priced cost for Claude Code, which has no AI Credits. A run that cannot be read or placed makes the figures unknown, with a reason, never 0. Claude Code runs started off the active branch (after an edit or rewind) are not counted. null means unknown, never zero \u2014 see unavailableReasons. `active`: true marks a session whose latest turn started in the last 15 minutes; its figures may still change. Cost figures carry their basis: billed (what GitHub Copilot billed, AI Credits), reported (what the agent logged itself, USD) and priced (tokens \u00d7 the price version in force on the turn's channel at the turn's time; see get_price_book, and priceVersionIds). The preferred figure is billed, else reported, else priced. A priced figure with apiEquivalent: true is what the same use costs on the API, though a flat-fee plan may have covered it. A priced figure with userPriceVersionIds used price versions the user added themselves (not bundled prices); say so when you quote it. An unknown figure is {known:false, reason}, never 0; totals give knownTurns of turns per basis. Currencies stay apart; `usd` converts only at 1 AI Credit = $0.01.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties